{"name":"Pink Bite","hex":"#e936a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"bite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut into something by clamping the teeth.","To hold something by clamping one's teeth."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of biting.","The wound left behind after having been bitten."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Biting","blocks":[{"text":"Biting is an action involving a set of teeth closing down on an object. It is a common zoological behavior, being found in toothed animals such as mammals, reptiles, amphibians, fishes, and arthropods. Biting is also an action humans participate in, most commonly when chewing food. Myocytic contraction of the muscles of mastication is responsible for generating the force that initiates the preparatory jaw abduction (opening), then rapidly adducts (closes) the jaw and moves the top and bottom teeth towards each other, resulting in the forceful action of a bite. Biting is one of the main functions in the lives of larger organisms, providing them the ability to forage, hunt, eat, build, play, fight, protect, and much more. Biting may be a form of physical aggression due to predatory or territorial intentions. In animals, biting can also be a normal activity, being used for eating, scratching, carrying objects, preparing food for young, removing ectoparasites or irritating foreign objects, and social grooming. Humans can have the tendency to bite each other whether they are children or adults."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Lion_Biting_Brother%27s_Tail_%2821277465378%29.jpg/330px-Lion_Biting_Brother%27s_Tail_%2821277465378%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biting"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/NIE_1905_Lion_-_teeth.jpg/330px-NIE_1905_Lion_-_teeth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/NIE_1905_Lion_-_teeth.jpg/330px-NIE_1905_Lion_-_teeth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Teeth of a lion, showcasing the front canines, middle carnassials, and back molars","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANIE_1905_Lion_-_teeth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Worker_ant_carrying_leaf.jpg/500px-Worker_ant_carrying_leaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Worker_ant_carrying_leaf.jpg/1280px-Worker_ant_carrying_leaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Worker_ant_carrying_leaf.jpg/500px-Worker_ant_carrying_leaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An ant carrying a leaf by biting it.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorker_ant_ca